{
  "_what": "PER-ANCHOR SWEEP of jess's four shipping grammars across parseman releases. One process per (anchor, dialect); every leg path-resolved into that anchor's own src/ through bench/jess/ab-hooks.mjs; both timed legs are `r<n>` sides so no leg can pick up HEAD. Extend this file by appending anchors — do not overwrite a row, and do not delete a DROPPED one.",
  "_method": {
    "harness": "a standalone per-anchor runner, NOT bench/jess/ab.ts — see notes/VERIFY-jess-ab.md",
    "legs": "two independent module graphs (r1, r2) of the SAME anchor, each timed ALONE, no interleave",
    "selfCheck": "selfCheckRatio is max/min of the two same-anchor legs. It must read ~1.00; an anchor above ~1.10 has its cross-anchor number VOIDED.",
    "sampling": "40 warmup parses, then 7 rounds x median of 5 timed repetitions; the reported ms is the median of the 7 round medians. ONE parse per repetition.",
    "loadGate": "refused above a 1-minute load average of 6 (grammars.ts LOAD_CEILING); the loadavg at each end is recorded per fixture.",
    "warning": "ab-hooks.mjs maps EVERY `h<n>` side to HEAD_SRC unconditionally. An `h<n>` leg handed an anchor path is a two-version chimera and read 44 ms against the same anchor's 17 ms. Use `r<n>` for both legs of an anchor."
  },
